the clark county school district  transition plan  seems to be creating more questions and  answers among educators and families  now the district released this 205 page  document last night  the proposal details how to bring staff  and students back to campus safely  with a hybrid model that's when students  attend class in person  two days and continue distance learning  at home the other three days  while it begins the process to bring  students back some remain  uncertain about the logistics it feels  like there was not  a very robust conversation with any  educators  because we've already found so many  holes in it things they haven't really  thought through  it's brought up so many questions some  questions include how educators may  teach students in person and online at  the same time  ccsd is also offering families the  choice to continue  full-time distance education we should  point out many private charter and  catholic schools  are doing hybrid learning and have been  for months we asked you on twitter do  you think ccsd has created a good return  plan  35 percent say yes 65 percent  say no
 

